{"schema_version":"1","event_id":"1bca8c303d0643e48244b595dae56954","incident_id":"bef03fb19987462c827f7e734546a349","ts":"2026-09-20T09:57:35.778635Z","stage":3,"kind":"triage","actor":"llm","summary":"ambiguous: H_meta vs H_db","payload":{"hypotheses":["H_meta","H_db"],"ambiguous":true,"triage":{"ambiguous":true,"reasoning":"The telemetry shows an ongoing severe outage: extremely high error rates at all service layers, high latency (svc.gateway.p99_ms ≈ 2.5x SLO), and orders.retry_ratio well above 4. All services and DB show consistently high latency (payments and db p99_ms ≈ 1.5s), and db.pool_busy_ratio is saturated (≈ 0.97). There are no change events or logs pointing to a deploy, and there is no indication of a single bad node. These patterns are consistent with both a self-sustaining retry storm (H_meta: as evidenced by the high retry_ratio and propagated high QPS to DB) and true underlying db capacity exhaustion or degraded state (H_db: high db query latency, pool saturation, continues even at 'steady' QPS). Only experiments that break the feedback loop or directly relieve DB can separate these. We cannot rule out either, and must propose measurable predictions for both.","hypotheses":[{"id":"H_meta","label":"metastable retry storm","description":"Runaway retries themselves, no longer an external trigger, are now saturating the DB and keeping the system unhealthy. Breaking the retry loop causes recovery that persists.","evidence":["svc.orders.retry_ratio is 4.0, well above normal, suggesting excessive retries.","db.pool_busy_ratio at 0.97 and query_p99_ms at 1.5s: consistent with call storm induced overload, not just intrinsic DB slowness.","All user metrics are equally impacted; could be consequence of retry feedback loop."]},{"id":"H_db","label":"degraded DB / capacity exhaustion","description":"The DB is persistently slow, pool is saturated at seemingly normal qps, and user-facing recovery only occurs if DB is directly relieved (e.g., via failover or further load shedding).","evidence":["db.qps is high, but not extreme versus historical (if known).","db.query_p99_ms, pool_busy_ratio both show the DB is persistently overloaded or degraded even without recent change events.","svc.retry_ratio could be secondary consequence of an intrinsically slow DB."]}],"predictions":[{"hypothesis_id":"H_meta","experiment_id":"retry_cap_0_20s","during":[{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"down"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"down"},{"metric":"db.qps","direction":"down"},{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"down"}],"after_release":[{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"flat"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"flat"},{"metric":"db.qps","direction":"flat"},{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"flat"}],"confirms_if":{"phase":"after_release","metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","expect":"within_baseline"}},{"hypothesis_id":"H_db","experiment_id":"retry_cap_0_20s","during":[{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"down"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"down"},{"metric":"db.qps","direction":"down"},{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"down"}],"after_release":[{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"up"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"up"},{"metric":"db.qps","direction":"up"},{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"up"}],"confirms_if":{"phase":"after_release","metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","expect":"up"}},{"hypothesis_id":"H_meta","experiment_id":"shed_10_20s","during":[{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"down"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"down"},{"metric":"db.qps","direction":"down"},{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"down"}],"after_release":[{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"flat"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"flat"},{"metric":"db.qps","direction":"flat"},{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"flat"}],"confirms_if":{"phase":"after_release","metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms",